[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2886038831","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106450#issuecomment-2886038831","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106450","id":2886038831,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sBXUv","user":{"login":"takethebait","id":50055051,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMDU1MDUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50055051?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait","html_url":"https://github.com/takethebait","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/takethebait/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-16T08:37:08Z","updated_at":"2025-05-16T08:47:24Z","body":"I can reproduce this issue on:\nGodot v4.5.dev (b7b3a1a78) - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7602) - AMD Ryzen 9 3900X 12-Core Processor (24 threads)\n\nI also get an error message once the bake is complete:\n```\nERROR: Parameter \"texture\" is null.\n   at: GLES3::TextureStorage::texture_get_texid (drivers\\gles3\\storage\\texture_storage.cpp:1795)\n```\n\nEdit: I can not reproduce this issue when switching to Forward+ rendering with Vulkan. In that case everything looks fine.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2886038831/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2892300747","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106450#issuecomment-2892300747","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106450","id":2892300747,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sZQHL","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-19T21:27:50Z","updated_at":"2025-05-19T21:43:46Z","body":"- Related to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/94406.\n\nThis appears to be due to the emission appearing way too strong in Compatibility compared to Forward+/Mobile. This is the case even if you switch the lightmap compression mode to Lossless to make sure it's not caused by VRAM compression. If you increase the bake quality, you'll notice how the emission looks more consistent:\n\nLow | Ultra\n-|-\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/85e419f7-5c70-4ab3-bd8c-7cf3ad245a92) | ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c1d5193d-8dca-454f-842c-c81171ad6757)\n\nForward+:\n\nLow | Ultra\n-|-\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3792d193-927b-4e05-a40a-d0525b42ac62) | ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/abf7b70f-5044-491d-ba33-1c769d74fc1e)\n\nI've multiplied the emission energy by 256 on the emission material and I get a result that's very close to Compatibility's overly strong emission:\n\nLow | Ultra\n-|-\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cd6fefab-2924-4be2-b6bb-7219174bcf40) | ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a3aa1d68-bdb1-4ccf-a896-6c1a5279980f)\n\nThis hints at an integer/float conversion issue somewhere in the Compatibility renderer code (e.g. when it's passing material data to the lightmapper).\n\nAs a bonus, here's what it'd look like with a lot more rays and supersampling:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dcb6def0-a335-449b-8d7d-fddca501685e)\n\nPS: In general, using high-energy emissive materials on very small objects will lead to poor results when baking lightmaps. Prefer using a relatively low emission energy, and add an OmniLight3D next to the emissive object with the Static GI mode instead.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2892300747/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3307182344","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106450#issuecomment-3307182344","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106450","id":3307182344,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FH5kI","user":{"login":"ToxicCrack","id":3591570,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1OTE1NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3591570?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToxicCrack","html_url":"https://github.com/ToxicCrack","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToxicCrack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToxicCrack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToxicCrack/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToxicCrack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToxicCrack/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToxicCrack/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToxicCrack/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToxicCrack/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToxicCrack/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-18T12:27:19Z","updated_at":"2025-09-18T12:27:33Z","body":"Is this going to be fixed? The issue is closed, but i still have this problem in 4.5 stable","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3307182344/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3308331109","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106450#issuecomment-3308331109","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106450","id":3308331109,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FMSBl","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-18T16:07:51Z","updated_at":"2025-09-18T16:08:08Z","body":"Reopening, as the original issue (emission in the lightmap being too strong in Compatibility) isn't fixed.\n\nAlso, we should document the caveat related to small emissive surfaces with strong emission causing visible noise in the baked lightmap (this also applies to SDFGI to an extent).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3308331109/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]